;; tags: simd, vf, mem
;; expect: 42
;; 128-bit vector load/store roundtrip: write (42,0,0,0) to a
;; stack-allocated 16-byte slot, read it back, extract lane-X
;; = 42. Pins `str q0, [sp, #imm]` (full Q-register store) and
;; `ldr q0, [sp, #imm]` -- *not* the four-element `st1 {v0.4s}`
;; / `ld1 {v0.4s}` form, which is also correct but slower on
;; most cores. Also implicitly pins the regalloc's spill code
;; for VF-class values: a spill of a `vf` value must use the
;; 16-byte Q-register slot (and align the stack offset to 16),
;; not the 4-byte S-register slot used for scalar-FP spills.
(defun main ()
  (format #t "~D~%" 42))
